  "logo": "https://cdn.uppromote.com/storage/uploads/logo/1775114961_8050523_163e4155843b208291578d61016ad258.png",
  "description": "<div style=\"font-family:Poppins;\"><div><p><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0981/6018/1588/files/Cryptosign_-_Polymer_Shares.jpg?v=1775054359\" style=\"width:300px;max-width:100%;\" class=\"fr-fic fr-dib\" alt=\"Cryptosign_-_Polymer_Shares.jpg?v=1775054359\"></p><p><b>• About our brand and products:</b>Cryptosign Hardware is a Belgium-based engineering lab specializing in military-grade physical backups for high-value digital assets. We manufacture premium aerospace Titanium Citadel Plates and custom hardware kits using Shamir’s Secret Sharing (SSS) to secure crypto seed phrases.</p><p><b>• What makes us different:</b>We solved the single-point-of-failure inherent in standard steel plates. Users split and encrypt their seed phrase locally via our air-gapped terminal. We only receive and blind-print the ciphertext payload. We have zero knowledge of the underlying keys, making our hardware mathematically impenetrable.</p><p><b>• How affiliates can earn:</b>Partners earn a baseline 15% commission on every sale. Because our high-ticket custom plates sell for €499, affiliates earn approximately €75 per conversion. We also offer custom coupon codes so you can incentivize your audience to buy today.</p><p><b>• How to promote us:</b>YouTubers and Twitter (X) OpSec auditors can promote us by reviewing our hardware, testing our air-gapped terminal, or comparing Cryptosign to legacy metal backups. We are happy to provide free physical test kits to qualified hardware reviewers.</p><p><b>• Other information:</b>We offer a 30-day cookie window and reliable, transparent payouts. Join the vanguard of Web3 hardware security and start monetizing your high-net-worth audience today.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0981/6018/1588/files/cryptosign_-_xa1.jpg?v=1775109593\" style=\"width:484px;max-width:100%;\" class=\"fr-fic fr-dib\" alt=\"cryptosign_-_xa1.jpg?v=1775109593\"></p></div></div>",
